{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" works like a dictionary with insertion-order iteration. Entities must conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID"},{"type":"text","text":" as the ID type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var cards = EntityStore<Card>()","","cards[card.id] = card                      \/\/ Insert or update — recorded","cards.modify(card.id) { $0.title = \"New\" } \/\/ In-place — recorded only if value changes","cards[card.id] = nil                       \/\/ Delete — recorded","","let card = cards[cardID]                   \/\/ O(1) lookup","let all  = cards.values                    \/\/ Insertion-ordered array","","cards.sort { $0.sortIndex < $1.sortIndex } \/\/ Only marks moved entities","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }          \/\/ Rebuilds index in one pass"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every mutation is tracked in a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":" that the middleware drains after each reducer call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Bulk Deletion","type":"heading","anchor":"Bulk-Deletion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cards[id] = nil"},{"type":"text","text":" shifts the storage array’s tail and reindexes the shifted entries — O(tail) per delete, so a loop of k subscript deletes costs O(n·k). To delete many entities at once, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(ids:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have the IDs) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(where:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (when you have a predicate) instead: both remove everything in a single pass with one index rebuild, record the same deletions, and cancel pending upserts exactly like the subscript."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["cards.remove(ids: selection)          \/\/ One pass, not a subscript loop","cards.removeAll { $0.isArchived }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"text":"Merging (Re-hydration)","type":"heading","anchor":"Merging-Re-hydration"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Replacing an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" after startup destroys any in-memory state that was loaded lazily after initial hydration. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead — entities only in the other store are always added, and the closure decides whether an incoming value overwrites the current one:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Absorb DB rows; take an incoming row only when the current one","\/\/ lacks lazily-computed data.","campaigns.merge(from: EntityStore(allFromDB)) { current, incoming in","    current.calculationState == nil && incoming.calculationState != nil","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge"},{"type":"text","text":" does not record changes — it has hydration semantics like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"reconcile vs merge","type":"heading","anchor":"reconcile-vs-merge"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two answer different questions:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"merge(from:shouldReplace:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Stance","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep everything, absorb what’s new","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage is authoritative ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"except"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" where you say otherwise","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removes rows","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Never","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When ","type":"text"},{"code":"removingMissing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the ID isn’t preserved","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Conflicts","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your closure decides, per pair","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage wins unless the ID is preserved","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile"},{"type":"text","text":" is what lets a remote edit or a remote deletion surface mid-session rather than waiting for the next launch. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" is the caller’s list of IDs that carry unflushed local intent; the store’s own un-drained "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"changes"},{"type":"text","text":" are folded in automatically, so a pending local deletion is never resurrected even when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["cards.reconcile(with: EntityStore(rowsFromDisk), preserving: dirtyIDs, removingMissing: true)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"merge"},{"type":"text","text":", it records no changes — every value it writes or removes already reflects what is in storage, so recording them would echo each remote change straight back as a local write."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most apps never call this directly; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator.rehydrate(into:)"},{"type":"text","text":" does, and computes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preserving"},{"type":"text","text":" for you."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"restore(from:)","type":"heading","anchor":"restorefrom"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" replaces all entities with those from the source store while recording the diff as changes for persistence. Used by undo\/redo (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deletions"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs in self but absent from source"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Upserts"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — IDs that are new or whose values differ"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unchanged"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — identical values produce no change records"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":3,"text":"Remote deletions are not undoable","type":"heading","anchor":"Remote-deletions-are-not-undoable"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One class of ID is skipped: anything "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reconcile"},{"type":"text","text":" removed because storage no longer held it. Those IDs are kept in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remotelyRemovedIDs"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"type":"text","text":" will neither re-add them nor record a change for them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without that, undo resurrects rows other devices deleted. An undo snapshot taken before the deletion still contains the entity, so restoring it records an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"upsert","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — which flushes as a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"creation","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and re-seeds every peer that had already agreed the row was gone. Undo is scoped to what the local user did; a deletion made on another device isn’t that."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An ID leaves the set as soon as it becomes local again — an explicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store[id] = entity"},{"type":"text","text":", or storage handing the row back on a later merge — so a row that another device deletes and then restores is undoable once more. The set survives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resetChanges()"},{"type":"text","text":", because a flush ends a pending write’s life, not a deletion’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ \"3 items were deleted on another device.\"","cards.remotelyRemovedIDs.count"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Stores that never sync never populate it, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"type":"text","text":" takes exactly the path it did before."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"EntityStore","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"],"title":"Reference","generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","abstract":[{"text":"Public API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","title":"ChangeSet","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","abstract":[{"text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoRedo":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo","abstract":[{"text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Undo \/ Redo"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","title":"Macros","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","abstract":[{"text":"API surface for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/keyvaluestoreguide","abstract":[{"text":"Persist scalar preferences like theme, sort order, or last-seen version — testably, with type-safe keys.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","title":"KeyValueStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"}}}